PATCH 621: retain the KDV framebuffer REP's CPU budget and write/scanout order (board:0034/0026).

Original 002b:7120..7134 clears DF, loads ESI from 6e88 and EDI from 0917,
loads ECX=16000, then REP MOVSD and RET. The old uncharged C loop writes the
whole aperture immediately. Use the shared original-backed REP path, which
completes each budget-sized write chunk before PIC resumes. Retire the four
setup instructions and RET at their real boundaries; do not inject elapsed time.

The complete original 11686:11696 trace reaches this copy during callback 168:
before 7120 cycle 350841173/budget 8827, before caller 6fcb cycle 350857178/budget
22822. REP chunks contain 8823 and 7177 dwords across TIMER_AddTick. The current
first unequal frame is 817; this proves its reached copy contract, while the
missing work before this copy remains a separate timing obligation. The test
compiles the actual ordered-patch 7120 body and checks the entire memory buffer
and clock against original DoString/PIC, including budget-one and tick boundaries.
--- a/fist_ext.c
+++ b/fist_ext.c
@@ -12156,3 +12156 @@
-  int iVar1;
-  undefined4 *puVar2;
-  undefined4 *puVar3;
+  /* 7120 CLD; 7121/7127 load ESI/EDI; 712d loads ECX=16000. */
@@ -12160,8 +12158,4 @@
-  puVar2 = DAT_0000_6e88;
-  puVar3 = DAT_0000_0917;
-  for (iVar1 = 16000; iVar1 != 0; iVar1 = iVar1 + -1) {
-    *puVar3 = *puVar2;
-    puVar2 = puVar2 + 1;
-    puVar3 = puVar3 + 1;
-  }
-  return;
+  fist_clock_charge_cpu_instructions(4);
+  fist_clock_rep_movs((uint8_t *)(uintptr_t)DAT_0000_0917,
+                      (const uint8_t *)(uintptr_t)DAT_0000_6e88, 4, 16000, 1);
+  fist_clock_charge_cpu_instructions(1); /* 7134 RET */
